  "goodToKnow": "Die Melodie is a melody or tune. The plural is die Melodien, pronounced me-lo-DEE-en. A tune you can't get out of your head is der Ohrwurm (earworm), a German word English borrowed. The melody of Germany's national anthem comes from Joseph Haydn's Kaiserhymne of 1797; only the third verse of the Deutschlandlied is sung today. Melodisch means melodic."
